 ],
 "literal": "With a sharp-edged striking-harpoon shining with metal-work / fitted to the front of a strong shaft of dried bamboo, / throwing it in the water-desert difficult to bear, with a pulling force, / as the fishermen in curved boats spear the horned shark, / the short-legged waterfowls that stayed on the long shore / disperse in white flocks from the seaside grove dense with flowers. / With the lord of such a shore of beautiful screwpines and cool water, / I indeed made a friendship that brings enmity!",
 "translation": "The fishermen in curved boats, using a pulling force, throw into the unbearable water-desert a sharp-edged harpoon, crafted with expert skill and fitted to the front of a strong shaft of dried bamboo, to spear the horned shark. At this, the short-legged waterfowls that stayed on the long shore disperse in white flocks from the seaside grove dense with fallen flowers. With the lord of such a shore of beautiful screwpines and cool waters, I indeed made a friendship that brings only enmity!",
 "modern": "கொல்லன் தொழிலால் சிறந்த கூர்மையான வாயைக் கொண்ட எறியும் உளியை, உலர்ந்த மூங்கிலின் வலிமையான தண்டின் நுனியில் பொருத்தி, தாங்குவதற்கு அரிய கடல் நீரில் வீசி, இழுக்கும் விசையோடு வளைந்த படகில் இருக்கும் பரதவர்கள் கொம்பையுடைய சுறா மீனை எறியும்போது, நீண்ட கரையில் இருந்த குட்டையான கால்களைக் கொண்ட அன்னப் பறவைகள், வெண்மையான கூட்டமாக மலர்கள் செறிந்த கடற்கரைச் சோலையிலிருந்து அஞ்சி ஓடும். அழகிய தாழை மரங்களையும் குளிர்ந்த நீரையும் உடைய கடற்கரைத் தலைவனுடன் நான் கொண்ட நட்பு, எனக்குப் பகையைத் தரும் நட்பாக முடிந்தது.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her friend (tōḻi) about her relationship with the hero, the lord of the maritime tract (neytal tiṇai). She describes how the fishermen in curved boats spear the horned shark using a sharp harpoon fitted to a strong bamboo shaft, causing the short-legged waterfowls on the shore to scatter in fear from the flower-dense groves. This vivid image of the peaceful birds being suddenly frightened and scattered by the violent hunt of the fishermen parallelly reflects her own situation: her peaceful life has been disrupted and shattered by her secret love affair with the hero. She laments that her friendship with the lord of the shore, which she hoped would bring happiness, has instead brought her only distress, gossip, and the enmity of her relatives. Key words include 'கோட்டுமீன்' (horned fish/shark), 'அன்னத்து வெண்தோடு இரியும்' (white flocks of waterfowls dispersing), and 'பகைதரு நட்பு' (enmity-bringing friendship).",
